{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #1092: declared status 'disproved'. Formalized: yes. Let $f_r(n)$ be maximal such that, if a graph $G$ has the property that every subgraph $H$ on $m$ vertices is the union of a graph with chromatic number $r$ and a graph with $\\leq f_r(m)$ edges, then $G$ has chromatic number $\\leq r+1$.\n\nIs it true that $f_2(n) \\gg n$? More generally, is $f_r(n)\\gg_r n$? Current best: Tang notes in the comments that a construction of R\\\"{o}dl \\cite{Ro82} disproves the first question, so that $f_2(n)\\not\\gg n$. Prize: no. Tags: chromatic number, geometry."},"claim_id":"vcl_e06314f650c376aa6f72b565583ee3c33890b2ac61523324b19f9e2a776485a0","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:1092","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_92584a831abf2d9f","object_root":"sha256:27493aaef7996b1f00ce0110cfeecddca94fd31375706439b15311ce064c6015","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:1092"}],"relations":[],"